# Backstage

Internal HRMS docs site (`apps/backstage`, port 5001). Next.js 16 App Router, no backend — markdown on disk is the product. Full layout is in `apps/backstage/AGENTS.md`.

## Content trees

| Folder | Served at | Edit how |
|---|---|---|
| `content/features/<menu-folder>/*.md` | `/features/<menu-folder>/<slug>` | `/document-feature` (overwrite OK) |
| `content/llm-wiki/**` | `/wiki/<path>` | `/sync-llm-wiki` only — never hand-edit |
| `content/wiki/*.md` | `/docs/<slug>` | Hand-authored; wiki-sync must not touch |

Adding a `.md` file is enough. Slugs come from `readdirSync` in `lib/docs.ts`, `lib/llm-wiki.ts`, `lib/features.ts`. Do not hardcode route lists.

## Feature guide shape

YAML may contain `confidence`, `last-analyzed`, `menu`, and optional `submenu`. `menu`/`submenu` match the HRMS left-nav; use `menu: Platform` when the feature is not in the sidebar. On disk, put the file in `content/features/<menu-folder>/` (`Leave & Attendance` → `leave-and-attendance`). `last-analyzed` is parsed (CRLF-safe) and shown under the H1 as `Last analyzed: YYYY-MM-DD`. Put sources in a trailing `## Reference` section, not in frontmatter — leftover `---` renders as a horizontal rule.

Section order: Overview → Workflow (mermaid flowchart) → Entry points → call chain → API endpoints → procs/tables → Table relationships (mermaid `erDiagram`) → Known gaps → Reference.

Write standard ```` ```mermaid ```` fences. `MermaidAwarePre` renders them; no app-specific syntax.

## Code

- Tailwind 4 + `prose`; **not** `@hrms/ui`.
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only for theme, nav, TOC, mermaid zoom.
- `params` is a `Promise` — `await params`. `generateStaticParams` on every dynamic page.
- Explicit `): React.JSX.Element`. Fresh `createSlugger()` per document (TOC ids must match heading ids).
- Import with `@/` (`@/lib/features`, `@/components/...`). No parent-relative `../`. Same-directory `./` is allowed.

```yaml
# ❌ BAD
sources:
  - lib/features.ts
# ✅ GOOD
---
confidence: high
last-analyzed: 2026-08-14
menu: Leave & Attendance
submenu: L&A Tasks
---
```
